# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, git converts LF to CRLF on Windows checkout, and this
# repository compares file BYTES in several places — pack payload digests,
# the `pack info` disclosure's "verbatim frontmatter block", the
# frontmatter `---` fences. Four separate Windows-only CI failures have
# come from that conversion, every one of them in test scaffolding that
# assumed an encoding rather than in the product, which handles both.
#
# The tests normalise as well. This is the belt; that is the braces.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes are bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.tgz binary
